+# tinyterraNodes Secure V2 source candidate
+
+These notes describe the composed `final-tiny-consumer-r2` source and selected `final-union-r1` SDK source. They do not describe an installed or admitted release. The original 43 node identities are retained, and four internal plot helpers are declared in source. Neither source composition nor a helper declaration establishes conversion completion.
+
+The selected source contains the graph, prompt, model, asset and output repairs described below. The current finite direct-native/default-SDK tuple has the scoped evidence recorded below; the installed Guest/service tuple and remaining purposes are not qualified by that batch. Earlier tests on other tuples remain scoped to those exact inputs and cases.
+
+## Registration and resource boundary
+
+`ComfyExtension` / `comfy_entrypoint` performs registration. Nodes declare `SDK_REFS` and their requested permissions; declarations are not deployment or user grants. Models, CLIP, VAE and upscale engines remain typed handles. Supported raw image, latent and composite buffers are materialized only through the SDK boundary. Asset catalogues and output destinations use logical names.
+
+The packaged `secure-nodes.json` is the exact saved normal-generator 47-entry output (43 original identities and four internal helpers), including 43 original validation declarations. Canonical packdb proxy/schema readback passed. Generation used dependency profile None; this does not establish private dependency installation, signed admission, grants or node behavior. No generator was rerun for packaging.
+
+## The original three pending service purposes
+
+| Original purpose | Selected source implementation | Remaining qualification |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ttN imageREMBG`: original U2Net background removal | The guest runs the genuine `rembg` U2Net path using a managed `background_removal/u2net.onnx` asset, bounded reads and exact size/checksums. The consumer retains its source image conversion, mask and output behavior. It does not substitute BiRefNet. | Resolve/install the reviewed guest dependency closure with the final trusted SDK, verify imports and native ABI, and compare actual offline U2Net inference and mask/output behavior with the original. |
+| `ttN multiModelMerge`: model and CLIP weighted sum / add difference | The handler uses public typed `weighted_add` calls for both model and CLIP, preserving selection branches, source loading and interpolation formulas. The selected SDK source implements those operations; they are no longer an API-absence refusal. | Qualify the final installed Guest/schema/ref/permission and cleanup paths against the original. The historical 216 passing genuine small-tensor native comparisons are component evidence for their tested source, not proof of the final installed tuple. |
+| `ttN advPlot images`: separate advanced branch image plotting | The continuation uses existing bounded `expand_upstream_variants`, selected literal axis compilation, four internal helpers and configuration substitution. Own catalogue markers and selected external widget descriptors use existing logical asset listing and the input-options broker. Selected hidden PROMPT JSON is carried through the normal Guest execution clone. | Bind an exact trusted profile, grants, targets, source/release/image/dependency pins and current catalogue values; validate the generated helper manifest; then qualify actual multi-cell graph/image/order/save/cancel behavior on the installed tuple. |
+
+The U2Net source requires Python 3.13, `rembg==2.0.67`, `onnxruntime==1.22.1`, `numpy==2.2.6`, and the CPU execution provider. The model is 175,997,641 bytes with SHA256 `8d10d2f3bb75ae3b6d527c77944fc5e7dcd94b29809d47a739a7a728a912b491`. Guest network denial and a pre-provisioned admitted model asset are required; the pack does not download model weights. The earlier common41/private28 publication is staging evidence, not final installed dependency or runtime proof.
+
+## Current graph profile and supported subset
+
+`GraphDomain.expand_nodes` and `expand_upstream_variants` exist in the selected source. It is incorrect to describe all upstream execution as a missing SDK operation. The named source profile is `tinyterra-image-plot-v1`; its trusted startup configuration, concrete target/widget/catalogue selections and actual release/runtime bindings are still required. A template or source profile name is not a deployed grant.
+
+The separate advanced branch plot supports admitted existing literal widgets on a selected direct linked upstream branch, within active-job budgets and source/rights checks. Caller mutation, replacement of linked inputs, insertion of omitted optional inputs and broader topology changes remain outside that selected subset. Configuration substitution and external input-options reads require their exact host selection. Ordinary direct-native input-options provider binding is not supported by this successor. Catalogue sentinel choices, if needed, require explicit review rather than implicit wildcard admission.
+
+## Seven named sampler purposes still partial in the current profile
+
+The following purpose-level limitations remain open and currently guarded. They do not refuse entire sampler nodes or declare the features permanently impossible, and missing resource metadata alone is not a formal purpose refusal.
+
+- **Embedded XY through sampler `adv_xyPlot`** remains guarded in `ttN pipeKSampler_v2`, its Advanced wrapper, `ttN pipeKSamplerSDXL_v2`, and `ttN KSampler_v2`. The native embedded path reruns the sampler caller with its input closure and preserves pipe/latent/grid/individual-save and executor-cache behavior. Those semantics exceed the selected upstream-literal branch authority, and these embedded sampler declarations do not enable that expansion. Disconnect `adv_xyPlot` for ordinary sampling, or use the separate advanced branch plot within its supported scope. Even an empty-axis no-op fallback is not implemented by the diagnostic change. Future work should first adapt a bounded continuation using existing APIs; any caller, linked or optional-input authority needs separate execution-owner review and native qualification.
+- **Legacy cross-render Hold** remains guarded in `ttN pipeKSampler`, its Advanced wrapper, and `ttN pipeKSamplerSDXL`. The native path reuses a prior successful live pipe and preview results; this consumer starts fresh sampler state per dispatch. Exact tenant/workflow/node/source identity, retained model/latent/ref lifetime, invalidation and release policy are not established for a prior-output slot. Select Sample to generate a new result. Pack globals or serialized live-ref tokens are not substitutes. A future host-owned retention feature must preserve Sample-then-Hold, failure/cancel isolation, and the native no-prior incoming-pipe/empty-UI fallback.
+
+Ordinary sampling with `adv_xyPlot=None` and legacy Sample branches remain available in source, subject to their other applicable qualifications. Changing five guard diagnostics does not implement either refused purpose or alter exception types or computation. Canonical purpose evidence and Root acceptance are maintained externally, rather than as per-node status files in the pack.
+
+## Other repairs present in the selected source
+
+- Nondefault tinyLoader discrete sampling and CFG rescale call the closed `model_sampling_discrete` and `rescale_cfg` transforms. Their selected SDK source delegates to the native algorithms. Final native/model/Guest parity remains a separate owner gate; these paths are not described as missing APIs.
+- `.tif` and `.tiff` use the TIFF encoder with the requested admitted suffix. `.rtf` uses the text-write path for the supplied string; it is not an added rich-text formatter. These source allowlist repairs still require final output and selected-platform encoding qualification.
+- Image overwrite uses an explicit `overwrite` option with `output.overwrite` rights and consent. The selected profile checks every declared class permission, so this imageOutput class requires `output.overwrite` consent even when the overwrite widget is False; supported False execution still uses the previous exclusive/skip behavior. The default remains new-only. Source includes exact-target checks, encoding before replacement and symlink/non-file refusal. Final collision, encoding-failure and native output qualification remain pending.
+- Text debug can read the linked source output label through the selected graph source-label operation. Its `graph` permission is explicit. This is not unrestricted workflow access.
+- Imported input management uses existing delete/copy operations with explicit `assets.import_url.manage` consent, exact current owner prefix and descriptor-relative nofollow checks. Reserved input copies require both source and target in the same owned import namespace. This service-source capability is not a general redesign of input or output ownership.
+
+## Wire boundary
+
+A `PIPE_LINE` / `PIPE_LINE_SDXL` carries its latent under `__ttn_latent__` on the wire and restores it to `samples` before computation. Otherwise the SDK treats a mapping containing `samples` as a single LATENT and hides the model bundle. Model/CLIP/VAE values remain independently typed handles. Other secure pipeline consumers must honor this convention.
+
+Hidden PROMPT transfer is selected, bounded JSON for the current admitted execution and normal ephemeral Guest class clone. It does not transfer DYNPROMPT, authentication state, live engine objects or arbitrary cross-render refs. Per-dispatch cleanup and exact manifest/rights/source checks remain required.
+
+## Evidence and frontend limits
+
+The historical merge differential, v4 graph/prompt unit components, later owned-import components and other owners' source checks each retain their own scope. Their counts are not added into a whole-pack pass. No installed SDK, complete Guest process, real U2Net inference or final multi-cell graph acceptance follows from source/AST checks alone.
